    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i added s3:ListBucket to the role and updated the resource to include the bucket arn itself too, but it's still throwing that access denied error. it feels like something is just blocking the path or intercepting the request right when it tries to go through. is there any other weird edge case in aws where a request just gets rejected even when the policy seems fine?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A very common edge case is cross-account access if your Lambda role or the bucket resides in a different AWS account. If that's not the case, another frequent culprit is a Service Control Policy (SCP) applied at the AWS Organization level, which overrides individual IAM policies. Finally, double-check the permissions of the principal identity; the Lambda execution role must match the principals allowed in any bucket policy.",
      "source": "target",
